Write the NSColor colorUsingColorSpaceName:device: case, which upstream left as a TODO.

It was the ONE case in the whole suite with no body: fifty lines of commented-out intentions and
then exit(1), so it fails in upstream CI too and this port counted it as "unwritten upstream"
rather than as a failure.

TASK #227 IS WHY IT IS WORTH WRITING NOW. CMake.app, a Qt application, dies intermittently at a
MEASURED 3 runs in 8 with

    -[__NSCFString colorUsingColorSpaceName:device:]: unrecognized selector

inside a NAMED colour conversion, and the receiver class differs between runs, which is freed
memory rather than a wrong type. A GUI race is a bad place to work on a lifetime bug. Upstream
TODO list even names the pair that matters, NSNamedColorSpace to NSDeviceRGBColorSpace.

WHAT IT ASSERTS, and deliberately not more: most of the pairs upstream listed have no portable
answer, because what a calibrated space converts to depends on a colour profile, and asserting
todays numbers would freeze an implementation detail rather than a contract. So this covers
  - a conversion to the space a colour is ALREADY in keeps every component exactly,
  - a grey converts to RGB channels that agree with each other, whatever the level is,
  - a NAMED colour converts WITHOUT RAISING, which is the #227 failure. nil is a legitimate
    answer for a name this system does not know and is not asserted against,
  - and a system colour retained across an autorelease pool drain is still usable, which is the
    shape a use-after-free would show up in.

MEASURED BOTH WAYS, because a case that passes silently proves nothing on its own: as written it
exits 0, and with one expected component changed from 0.25 to 0.99 it exits 134, the assertion
aborting. So it does exercise the code.

IT PASSES, and that is a real result rather than a fix: the deterministic path is clean, so
whatever kills Qt is not reachable from a headless conversion of a system colour. #227 keeps the
GUI rate as its measurement.

scripts/gen-testsuite-buck.py drops it from UPSTREAM_PLACEHOLDERS in the same change, or a case
that now passes would go on being excluded from the count.

